# The code role's mint dispatcher. This load block mirrors `mine.tree`'s: one sibling mint per statement head,
# named for the rule whose captures it mints. It was MISSING until 2026-08-31, which meant the merged mint
# grammar held exactly one rule (`mint code`) and every `case x, mint y` below dangled. Nothing reported it
# because nothing ran the mint side (mint-bridge-0001).
#
# Four heads have no mint yet and so are not loaded: `book`, `kink`, `cast` and `zone`. `pnpm term:mint-parity`
# names them, and they close as part of mint-bridge-0003.


mint code
  case form
    site form
  case task
    site task
  case call
    site call
  case hook
    site hook
  case host
    site host
  case load
    site load
  case dock-bind
    site dock-bind
  case bind-def
    site bind-def
  case rule, mint rule-def
    site rule
  case roll, mint roll-def
    site roll
  case dock
    site dock
  case test
    site test
  case hold
    site hold
  case suit
    site suit
  case mask
    site mask
  case wear
    site wear
  case bear
    site bear
  case book
    site book
  case tree
    site tree
  case kink
    site kink
  case fuse
    site fuse
  case beam
    site beam
  case slot
    site slot
  case note
    site note
  case halt
    site halt
  case save
    site save
  case seed
    site seed
  case lace
    site lace
  case cast
    site cast
  case tune
    site tune
  case view, mint view-def
    site view
